# SegmentedControl

> Lede 0.7.1's docs for SegmentedControl, installed with it. Setup, and every item in the release: [README.md](README.md). Online: https://lede.cloudcompute.com/reference/segmented-control.md

A native `<fieldset>` of radio inputs, with a thumb that slides to the checked option.

## Install

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add @lede/segmented-control
```

The command needs Lede's registry in `components.json`, as [README.md](README.md#use-it-in-a-shadcn-project) shows. It also installs the items [`lede-theme`](lede-theme.md) and [`lede-utils`](lede-utils.md). The item's JSON, with each file's source, is https://lede.cloudcompute.com/r/v0.7.1/segmented-control.json.

## Import

```tsx
import { SegmentedControl } from '@/components/lede/segmented-control';
```

## Files and exports

| Installs to | Import from | Exports |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `components/lede/segmented-control.tsx` | `@/components/lede/segmented-control` | `SegmentedControl` (component), `SegmentedOption` (type), `SegmentedControlProps` (type) |

## Props

A native `<fieldset>` of radio inputs: arrow keys, form submission and screen-reader semantics come from the browser. It fits the width its container gives it, narrowing its labels' insets and then stacking them. An `auto` grid track that holds it, or a flex item holding it without `min-width: 0`, gives it its labels' full width, so it can't fit. `name`, `form` and `required` go on each radio; other HTML attributes and `ref` go on the `<fieldset>`.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `label` (required) | `string` |  | The group's accessible name, rendered as a visually hidden `<legend>`. |
| `options` (required) | `Array<SegmentedOption \| string>` |  |  |
| `value` | `string` |  |  |
| `defaultValue` | `string` |  |  |
| `onValueChange` | `(value: string) => void` |  |  |
| `name` | `string` |  | Form field name. Defaults to a generated id. |
| `form` | `string` |  | The form the radios belong to, by id, when the control sits outside it. |
| `required` | `boolean` |  | A choice is needed before the form submits. |
| `size` | `'sm' \| 'md'` |  |  |
| `block` | `boolean` |  |  |

SegmentedControl also takes the attributes of `<fieldset>`, such as `className`.

## Example

The smallest working use, from the docs site:

```tsx
import { useState } from 'react';
import { SegmentedControl } from '@/components/lede/segmented-control';

export function RangePicker() {
  const [range, setRange] = useState('Week');
  return <SegmentedControl label="Range" options={['Day', 'Week', 'Month']} value={range} onValueChange={setRange} />;
}
```

Docs: [Components](https://lede.cloudcompute.com/components.md).

